@1 = ~Interesting. I don't recall inviting guests over to my room, and YES, this is MY room in case you haven't noticed.~
@2 = ~My apologies for intrusion. Pardon my asking but... you look peculiar.~
@3 = ~Allow me to simply raid your drawers and take any valuables you have and you WON'T call the guards. Trust me.~
@4 = ~We're leaving.~
@5 = ~Observant. Truly. Don't overstay your welcome just because you find me alluring. Hmm… hold on a second. You look the adventurer type. Seeking wealth, slaughtering monsters… maybe people? Am I right?~
@6 = ~Well, we are adventurers. We perform certain tasks. It depends what you have on your mind.~
@7 = ~We enjoy bloodshed, if this is what you mean. Why?~
@8 = ~No. We are simple merchants, armed to defend ourselves against bandits. That is all.~
@9 = ~Lovely. You are just the merry band of misfits I could use. My name is Astarion.~
@10 = ~Magnificent. Then our cooperation shall be fruitful for both sides. My name is Astarion.~
@11 = ~My master will be pleased. Listen up, this job required discretion. We do not want to alarm Flaming Fist now, do we? My... well, your assignment is fairly simple. There is a lonely art dealer called Derek, living in northwest part of Baldur's Gate. He recently lost his fortune due to gambling. An obtuse, lazy and somewhat foolish idiot who thought he can defeat death by bargaining with C. He caught attention of the wrong string-puller.~
@12 = ~I command his determination, but what I cannot stand are his selfish machinations and the lies he perpetrated whilst promising my master that he will get what he is due. What WE were due. You do not need to know the details of our agreements as it isn't in public interest. Target is located in a small house to the left from gate entrance to Silvershield's estate.~
@13 = ~Your job is to simple. No sugar-coating. Kill him and bring me his body. I don't care how you do it. I offer you 6000 gold coins for the job.~
@14 = ~Are you crazy?! You want us to kill an innocent person over something we don't even know? I refuse to do your dirty work.~
@15 = ~Tempting. How about you lift the price up to 10000?~
@16 = ~Bloody work. Something just for me. I'll do it.~
@17 = ~And I was beginning to see you as more than a gutless coward. Fine, leave me be then. No deal.~
@18 = ~Dancing with the devil guarantees a spot in Nine Hells. Master C may be wealthy but he isn't willing to part with his gold with just anyone. Besides… he doesn't necessarily know that I am hiring someone to do my dirty work. And let's let it stay that way.~
@19 = ~That's more like it. I'm beginning to like you, <CHARNAME>. Yes, I do know your name. I recognised you the moment you walked in. I recognised you from the start. Information travels remarkably fast here in this city. Do remember - double crossing me will lead you to your grave. It is a tiny bit too late to back away now. Go on.~
@20 = ~Anymore Questions?~
@21 = ~Are you… a vampire?~
@22 = ~Who is this master C?~
@23 = ~Isn't there a more peaceful resolution?~
@24 = ~Thank you. That's all I wanted to ask.~
@25 = ~This question was throbbing in your throat since you walked in, didn't it? I believe we both know the answer.~
@26 = ~This information is classified. Knowing about him would put you in danger… and me.~
@27 = ~If you want to play the saint you shouldn't have agreed. This is a bloody work and requires subterfuge, not a brittle heart. Kill your target, bring me the body, get your reward and we go separate ways. This is it.~
@28 = ~I knew something was wrong from the moment we walked in here and this vile request only added to my suspicion. <CHARNAME>, I will not have anything to do with a murder! It's the most immoral, repulsive deed to be done.~
@29 = ~As long as we get paid at the end of the day, I'm all in.~
@30 = ~I sincerely h-hope you are not entertaining th-th-the idea of going through with that.~
@31 = ~Compelling offer, rivvin. <CHARNAME>, it's your choice but I personally don't see a valid reason to refuse.~
@32 = ~Be careful, my friend. I recognise this manner of creature. Pale skin, red eyes and that particular scent. It appears to be a vampire and they are not to be trusted. But I leave the choice to you.~
@33 = ~I put much faith in you, <CHARNAME> and you practically backstabbed me. I will not allow such evil to exist, nor will I let you murder an innocent. Our partnership is over.~

@47 = ~Derek's Body~
@48 = ~The body of Derek, the unfortunate art dealer who crossed a vampire lord and paid the price. It is proof that the target was killed. Handle it with care.~

@34 = ~Welcome back, my delicious appetizer. How's the hunt going?~
@35 = ~We killed him.~
@36 = ~He ran away before we could get him.~
@37 = ~We decided not to work for you anymore.~
@38 = ~You did not disappoint, my love. I was wondering if you'd be coming back with his actual body. You played your role well. Now… I'm afraid I have to kill you. Nothing personal. You know too much. Master C will bury me again. For longer than a year this time, that bastard! Just stand still, and let me suck your blood out!~
@39 = ~I see. Well, that is most disappointing. Especially that… your attempt at thwarting my plans is futile. Derek didn't make it past the city gates before 'they' got to him. He is no longer with us, poor sod.~
@40 = ~Then what's the point of that charade? Why did you send us against Derek if he wouldn't make it out alive anyway?~
@41 = ~Because it's thrilling. I was about to head out to deal with Derek when you first walked into my room. Then I saw an opportunity and I just couldn't resist the temptation. Having you do the dirty work for me, handing me my reward on a silver platter and then… allowing me to consume your blood as a cherry on the top. Perfect plan... you derailed the progression a bit but in the end... you're mine now. Stand still and let me drink your blood, my little treat.~
@42 = ~I understand. Well, all good things come to an end eventually. Luckily for me, this will be a VERY good thing for me to experience.~
@60 = ~We returned to Astarion with Derek's body. He revealed that the entire bargain had been a trap and attacked us.~
@61 = ~We refused to continue working for Astarion. He turned on us and attacked.~
